<title>USA: Ford recalls 40,134 Mercury Villagers.</title>
<headline>Ford recalls 40,134 Mercury Villagers.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co said Wednesday it was recalling 40,134 Mercury Villagers because of a potential problem with the rear taillamp.</p>
<p>On some of the vehicles, the rear combination brake and taillamp sockets may expand to the point that the metal sleeve could be pushed out to the surrounding plastic socket housing. If this were to occur, it could result in a loss of electrical continuity between the bulb and the electrical contact plate, causing an intermittent or inoperable rear taillamp, Ford said.</p>
<p>It said 2,140 of the recalled vehicles are in Canada.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
